      "writtenOn": "2022-07-28T18:38:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t love having duplicate enums with slight differences - Brian, is that what you were proposing?\n\nI guess having only one of them an `enum class` makes it so you cannot convert between them, but it seems kind of funny that they\u0027re different?\n\nThinking about this some more, though, we arguably have a reason for `UNDEFINED` in `CTSRelaxed` - that won\u0027t always be used. (I\u0027m not clear on why we need it for `Enforced`.) And maybe it doesn\u0027t need `FUTURE`? Maybe that\u0027s a (separate from type safety) reason to have both `enum`s?\n\nThe reason I see for `UNDEFINED` in Relaxed is if there are no levels on which we run workarounds. But that\u0027s no different from them being set to the same value, right?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 26,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 30,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "596f896719a0a495974372831f031670db30f030",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
